index 4479b53..5e56fe8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,45 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Signed-in readers can open **My account** → **Sign-in & security** at
+`/devtools-times/account/settings` to create, rename, and remove passkeys. Password
+sign-in continues to use the existing Times login service, now through a same-origin
+endpoint that establishes an HttpOnly Astro session. The service must return a
+nonempty `token` on successful authentication. Its `user.id` (or `userId`) is used
+as the stable account subject; the demo fallback is its unique, stable username.
+Passwords and upstream tokens are never persisted by this application.
+
+Passkeys are verified with SimpleWebAuthn, require user verification, and store only
+public credential material. Credential IDs and mutations are scoped to the signed-in
+reader and relying-party domain. Account responses disable caching; mutations check
+the request Origin. Registration and authentication challenges expire after five
+minutes, and reader sessions expire after 24 hours.
+
+Runtime configuration:
+
+- Use Node.js **22.13 or later** (the credential store uses `node:sqlite`).
+- Set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the public HTTPS origin, such as
+  `https://astro-news-pytrpecapa-uc.a.run.app`, without the `/devtools-times` path.
+  Set this explicitly behind a reverse proxy. Localhost is supported for development.
+- Set `PASSKEY_DB_PATH` to a durable SQLite path. It defaults to
+  `.data/passkeys.sqlite`. Preserve this file across deployments, along with Astro's
+  session storage. SQLite and the default filesystem session driver suit a single
+  instance; a deployment with multiple instances needs shared account and session
+  storage. Ephemeral Cloud Run filesystems do not preserve passkeys across restarts.
+
+The browser receives the complete remaining credential list after a successful
+load or mutation, including an empty list when the last passkey is removed, using
+[`signalAllAcceptedCredentials`](https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/#sctn-signalAllAcceptedCredentials).
+Account names are refreshed using `signalCurrentUserDetails` where available.
+Individual passkey display names are site labels; WebAuthn does not offer a signal
+to rename individual keys in a device's password manager. Browser signals are
+best effort and only run after the server confirms account state. Unsupported
+browsers and failed signals show instructions for manual password-manager cleanup;
+failed signals can be retried without repeating the account mutation.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for credential ownership, persistence, validation, origin enforcement,
+and browser-sync tests, and `pnpm build` to compile the app. These checks do not
+start a server or require browser verification.
